course: dictionary
lesson: 4885
title: The letters ie and i.e.
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The short form i.e. is a signal word. It tells you that the next words will explain more exactly what was just said. «The largest planet, i.e. Jupiter, has a famous red spot.» Here i.e. tells you that Jupiter is the planet being named.
explain: To check, swap in the meaning: «The largest planet, in other words Jupiter, has a famous red spot.» The sentence still makes sense, so i.e. means in other words, or that is.
explain: Ie is also a pair of letters inside many English words. You will see it in «believe» and «relief». The spelling rule is i before e, except after c, but there are exceptions such as «weird» and «science», so always check.
fact: i.e. is short for the Latin id est, which means that is or in other words.
fact: i.e. comes before a clearer explanation of what was just said.
fact: .ie is the internet ending for websites from Ireland.
fact: ie is a common pair of letters in English words, as in «believe».
fact: The spelling rule is i before e except after c, as in «receive», but «weird» and «science» break it.
exercise: «The largest planet, i.e. Jupiter, has a famous red spot.» What does i.e. mean here? | in the opposite direction | a type of spaceship | a large number of planets | *in other words
exercise: Which ending belongs to websites from Ireland? | *.ie | .com | .uk | .org
exercise: Which word follows the i before e rule? | weird | science | *believe | friend
test: «The bus was late, i.e. it did not arrive until after nine.» What does i.e. do in this sentence? | It starts a brand new story | It is a spelling mistake | *It explains more exactly what was just said | It says the bus was early
test: Which word breaks the i before e rule? | piece | *weird | relief | believe
exam: What is i.e. short for? | in example | *id est, a Latin phrase meaning that is | International Edition | Italy and England
